{"ref":"BDB, מַבּוּעַ²","hw":"מַבּוּעַ²","html":"† <big><span dir=\"rtl\">מַבּוּעַ</span></big>  <strong>n.</strong>[<strong>m.</strong>] <strong>spring</strong> of water <strong>(</strong>Assyrian <em>nambaʾu</em> Dl<sup>HWB 442</sup>, Arabic <span dir=\"rtl\">مَنْبَعٌ</span>, Syriac <span dir=\"rtl\">ܡܰܒܽܘܥ</span> <strong>)</strong>;—abs. <span dir=\"rtl\">מ׳</span> <a data-ref=\"Ecclesiastes 12:6\" href=\"/Ecclesiastes.12.6\">Ec 12:6</a>; pl. cstr. <span dir=\"rtl\">מַבּעֵי מַיִם</span> <a data-ref=\"Isaiah 35:7\" href=\"/Isaiah.35.7\">Is 35:7</a>; <a data-ref=\"Isaiah 49:10\" href=\"/Isaiah.49.10\">49:10</a> (for returning exiles).","next":"BDB, נִבְשָׁן²","prev":"BDB, נָבַע"}